// What horse behaviour patterns mean — from open-access veterinary sources.
//
// Every pattern cites the sources it rests on (ids in SOURCES). Where no source
// gives a number, the entry says so: thresholds EquiCare uses in those places
// are our operational choice, marked `ours: true`, and belong in front of a vet.
// `equicare` says honestly what the system can observe today:
//   measured     — read by the camera now
//   prototype    — a camera heuristic exists but is not validated on horses
//   label        — no detector yet; staff mark it on footage to teach one
//   sensor       — needs other hardware (IMU, flow meter)
//   not_visible  — a stall camera at 3–4 m cannot see it
// Compiled 2026-09-27 from ~55 open-access sources; extended 2026-10-04 from a
// six-part review (rest, pain, vices and welfare, feeding and heat, monitoring
// studies, communication and the Indian context) — about 120 sources more.
// Paywalled originals are cited through their abstracts (access: "abstract")
// or the open papers that describe them.

